 "missing": [],
 "notes": "Native chunk storage is a flat struct in world.h with a section mask, reached through an open-addressing map of chunk pointers plus a 256-slot direct-mapped cache (world.h struct world): a pointer graph and heap allocation per chunk, relevant to the GPU contract. The chunk-level entity and tile-entity plumbing is spread across serverreplay.c, item_entity.c, living.c and world.c and was only spot-checked. Closed by lane/idxworld: the per-family section lists are one list in effect (each family's entries carry the insertion stamp the shared list would order them by, and the queries merge the families section by section by it: entityquery.h); the client-side members are equivalent or without effect (the member notes). lastSaveTime and isModified only decide what a save writes, which no running state reads. getBiomeGenForWorldCoords' 0xFF fallback (a column with no stored biome) is unreachable here: every chunk the 1.7.10 server generates or reads carries its Biomes array, and a full chunk packet carries it to the client."
}
